// Signing configuration for the Panoptos app target.
//
// The developer's Apple team is supplied by an optional local file so the
// project does not have to name one person's account. The team ID is not a
// secret: it is embedded in the code signature of every shipped build and is
// readable with `codesign -dvvv`. Keeping it out of tracked files means anyone
// building Panoptos signs with their own account without editing a file that
// everyone else also edits.
//
// #include? does not fail when the file is absent, so a checkout without one
// still builds. Debug defaults to ad-hoc signing; a local certificate override
// gives Accessibility approval a stable signer across rebuilds. Release needs a
// real Developer ID, and scripts/release.sh reports the missing file directly.
// Panoptos has no app-specific Keychain entitlement, so Release does not need
// a provisioning profile for application data-protection access.
PANOPTOS_DEBUG_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = $(PANOPTOS_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM)
